/*
 * ============================================================================
 *  Branding — RoomOS branding macro (configurable asset hosting)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *  WHAT IT DOES
 *  ------------
 *  Adds a PIN-protected "Branding" button letting on-site administrators apply
 *  their own logo, halfwake logo, wallpaper and welcome message.
 *
 *  Assets are organised one folder per customer / entity:
 *
 *      <asset base URL>/<customer id>/logo.png
 *      <asset base URL>/<customer id>/halfwake.png
 *      <asset base URL>/<customer id>/wallpaper.jpg
 *
 *  ASSET TYPES — WHAT IS WHAT
 *    logo.png       -> LOGO shown in awake mode          (Type: Branding)
 *    halfwake.png   -> LOGO shown on the halfwake screen (Type: HalfwakeBranding)
 *    wallpaper.jpg  -> the only BACKGROUND image         (Type: Background)
 *  There is no separate halfwake background: RoomOS owns that screen's backdrop.
 *
 *  WELCOME MESSAGE
 *  ---------------
 *  Handled here too, but it is NOT an image: it lives in
 *  xConfiguration UserInterface CustomMessage. Setting it is instant (no
 *  download). The staged value is stored in BrandingData so it can be re-applied
 *  remotely together with the images.
 *
 *  TWO WAYS TO APPLY — BOTH MANUAL
 *  -------------------------------
 *    1. From the touch panel: Branding > Apply (per asset) or Apply all
 *    2. From the web interface / API: activate the dormant macro BrandingApply
 *
 *  Nothing is ever applied automatically: no fetch at init, at restart, or on a
 *  schedule. RoomOS keeps the images locally once applied.
 *
 *  ASSET HOSTING — RESOLUTION ORDER (first non-empty wins)
 *  ------------------------------------------------------
 *    1. Per-asset override   "Edit" button on that row
 *    2. Asset server         "Set" button on the Asset server row
 *    3. ASSET_BASE_URL       constant below (fleet-wide default)
 *    4. GitHub               GITHUB_* constants (LAB / TROUBLESHOOTING ONLY —
 *                            raw.githubusercontent.com is frequently blocked on
 *                            corporate networks and is rate-limited; prefer
 *                            GitHub Pages, an internal web server or Azure Blob
 *                            Storage in production)
 *
 *  HOSTING REQUIREMENTS
 *  --------------------
 *    - HTTP or HTTPS only (Branding Fetch accepts nothing else)
 *    - Reachable WITHOUT authentication (devices send no credentials)
 *    - Must return the binary image, not an HTML preview page
 *      -> SharePoint / OneDrive / Google Drive share links do NOT work: they
 *         return an HTML preview, use redirect chains and expiring tokens, and
 *         their per-user authentication cannot be satisfied by a device
 *
 *  ASSET SPECIFICATIONS
 *  --------------------
 *    logo.png       transparent PNG, ~272x272 px, <= 1 MB
 *    halfwake.png   transparent PNG, ~272x272 px, <= 1 MB
 *    wallpaper.jpg  JPEG/PNG, 3840x2160 px (4K) recommended, <= 16 MB
 *    message        plain text, <= MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH characters
 *
 *  REQUIREMENTS
 *  ------------
 *    - RoomOS 11 or later, ES modules, Transpile = False
 *    - This macro must stay ACTIVE
 *    - BrandingData must stay dormant (settings + session storage)
 *    - BrandingApply must stay dormant (remote trigger, activate to fire)
 *
 *  PARAMETERS TO REVIEW BEFORE USE
 *  -------------------------------
 *    PIN                     MANDATORY — replace 'CHANGE_ME'. The panel refuses
 *                            to unlock while it still is the default value.
 *    ASSET_BASE_URL          fleet-wide asset server
 *    GITHUB_*                lab fallback only
 *    FILE_NAMES              expected file names inside each customer folder
 *    KNOWN_CUSTOMERS         optional shortlist shown as quick-pick buttons
 *    ADMIN_SESSION_MINUTES
 *    SHOW_BUTTON_IN_CALL     true (default) -> button also visible during calls
 *    KEEP_SESSION_IN_CALL    true (default) -> session survives call start
 *    CLEAR_MESSAGE_WITH_BRANDING
 *
 *  IMPORTANT NOTES
 *  ---------------
 *    - Control Hub supports only ONE global branding per organisation. A global
 *      branding pushed there overrides what this macro applies — re-apply
 *      manually when that happens.
 *
 *  FIRST RUN
 *  ---------
 *    1. Set PIN, then ASSET_BASE_URL (or the GITHUB_* constants).
 *    2. Publish the images to <base>/<customer id>/.
 *    3. On the panel: Branding > set the Customer ID > Apply all.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */

